   $q$A company is designing an open top box with a square base that must hold exactly 32 cubic feet. Which base side and height use the least cardboard for the base and four sides?$q$, $q$[{"text":"base side 4 ft, height 2 ft","is_correct":true},{"text":"base side 1 ft, height 32 ft","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-smallest-base"},{"text":"base side 2 ft, height 8 ft","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-tallest-box"},{"text":"base side 8 ft, height $0.5$ ft","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"chose-widest-base"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$base side 4 ft, height 2 ft$q$, $q$Each box holds 32 cubic feet, and the cardboard is $s^2 + 4sh$: $16 + 32 = 48$ for the 4 ft base, compared with 68, 80 and 129 square feet for the others. The choice with the 8 ft base looks efficient because it is short, but its large base alone uses 64 square feet.$q$, 'draft', null)
