   $q$A steel pipe is a hollow cylinder 100 cm long with an outer radius of 5 cm and an inner radius of 4 cm. Steel has a density of $7.8$ g per cubic centimeter. Using $3.14$ for $\pi$ and rounding to the nearest tenth, what is the mass of the pipe in kilograms?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$61.2$ kg","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-hollow-center"},{"text":"$2.4$ kg","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-radii-before-squaring"},{"text":"$22.0$ kg","is_correct":true},{"text":"$220.4$ kg","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"converted-grams-wrong"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$22.0$ kg$q$, $q$The steel volume is $\pi(5^2 - 4^2)(100) = 900\pi \approx 2{,}826$ cubic centimeters, so the mass is $2{,}826 \cdot 7.8 = 22{,}042.8$ g, or about $22.0$ kg. The choice $2.4$ kg squares the difference $5 - 4 = 1$ instead of subtracting the squares.$q$, 'draft', null)
